WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.769
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Monday, October twenty sixth.

2
00:00:04.769 --> 00:00:12.323
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.323 --> 00:00:15.451
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:17.493
We start in Nigeria.

5
00:00:17.493 --> 00:00:23.357
On Friday, October twenty third, gunmen on motorcycles attacked the village of Binnari, in the Karim Lamido area of Taraba State.

6
00:00:23.357 --> 00:00:31.214
BBC Africa and The Guardian Nigeria report police say at least ten people were killed, and witnesses say the toll could be much higher.

7
00:00:31.214 --> 00:00:37.999
Channels Television reports at least thirty seven confirmed dead, and Amnesty International says at least forty were killed.

8
00:00:37.999 --> 00:00:40.596
Shops were looted and homes set on fire.

9
00:00:40.596 --> 00:00:50.786
In Saudi Arabia, the Institute for the Study of War and the Critical Threats Project report the Houthis have fired at least twelve missiles and two drones at Saudi Arabia since Saturday.

10
00:00:50.786 --> 00:01:07.978
Australia's Smartraveller says it continues to advise Do Not Travel to Saudi Arabia, and not to travel to King Khalid International Airport in Riyadh, King Fahd International Airport in Dammam, or Abha International Airport, because recent security incidents are disrupting airport operations.

11
00:01:07.978 --> 00:01:18.038
In India, Reuters reports two states on the eastern coast are preparing to evacuate thousands of people ahead of Cyclone Arnab, which is expected to make landfall on Wednesday.

12
00:01:18.038 --> 00:01:23.053
One of the states says it will close schools in some districts for two days.

13
00:01:23.053 --> 00:01:30.866
In Ukraine, Reuters reports President Zelenskiy says US warnings of imminent Russian ballistic missile strikes have been fully restored after recent issues.

14
00:01:30.866 --> 00:01:37.289
Officials say Russian strikes injured six people in the Zaporizhzhia and Chernihiv regions.

15
00:01:37.289 --> 00:01:43.616
Inside Russia, the governor of the Voronezh region says a drone attack killed two men.

16
00:01:43.616 --> 00:01:45.765
A few updates on stories we've covered.

17
00:01:45.765 --> 00:01:57.468
Update on the church attack in Jordan: Reuters reports, citing state television, that Jordanian security forces have arrested three suspects in the October twenty third attack in the Karak area, which killed nine people.

18
00:01:57.468 --> 00:02:07.262
Update on Ebola: Reuters reports Nigeria's Ebola patient has been medically evacuated to Switzerland, and the Africa C D C says scientists will investigate where the Nigeria case came from.

19
00:02:07.262 --> 00:02:17.139
Uganda says citizens returning with a history of travel to the Democratic Republic of the Congo will be quarantined for twenty one days, according to Reuters and BBC Africa.

20
00:02:17.139 --> 00:02:20.286
Now a few quick notes by region.

21
00:02:20.286 --> 00:02:33.795
In Africa, NewsPoint Nigeria and Dawn Herald report bandits killed seven members of a local vigilante group and abducted dozens of residents in an overnight raid on Kaura Namoda, in Zamfara State, starting Friday, October twenty third.

22
00:02:33.795 --> 00:02:47.324
In South Asia, Pakistan's military media wing says security forces killed six militants in an operation in Zarkani, in Dera Ismail Khan district, on Saturday, October twenty fourth, and that two soldiers were killed.

23
00:02:47.324 --> 00:02:54.426
In the Pacific, Smartraveller says Vanuatu's Ministry of Health has declared an influenza A outbreak in Port Vila and on Efate Island.

24
00:02:54.426 --> 00:03:03.109
In Europe, Radio Free Europe reports Serbia's Aleksandar Vucic conceded defeat to the student led protest movement in yesterday's parliamentary elections.

25
00:03:03.109 --> 00:03:07.586
Final results have not yet been announced.

26
00:03:07.586 --> 00:03:18.560
On sanctions, a Reuters exclusive reports how Myanmar disguised purchases of sanctioned Iranian jet fuel, including a December twenty twenty five delivery by the US sanctioned tanker Reef.

27
00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.034
That's today's brief.

28
00:03:20.034 --> 00:03:28.107
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

29
00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:36.333
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

30
00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.411
This brief is digitally narrated.

31
00:03:38.411 --> 00:03:39.341
Questions?

32
00:03:39.341 --> 00:03:42.670
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

33
00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:44.707
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
